  "summary": "Monday 10/26 CT list at St. Brigid Imaging is ready. Four studies are booked. Three cancelled appointments were skipped (appt-00006, appt-00001, appt-00008).\n\n1. pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast. Ordered (sr-t0001). He has diabetes and his last creatinine (09/24) was more than 30 days old, so I ordered a creatinine before the scan (sr-t0005). An outside creatinine arrived while I worked: 1.52 on 10/22, up from 0.94. That is eGFR about 64 and not acute kidney injury by the policy's definition, so the decision stays. The pre-scan creatinine is still in place as a recheck. Patient message comm-t0011; follow-up task for you (task-t0030).\n\n2. pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast, pancreatic cyst. Ordered (sr-t0002). The 2019 day-of radiology report grades his iohexol reaction moderate; the \"anaphylaxis\" allergy-list label is the patient's own report and doesn't change that grade under the policy. Premedication is ordered: prednisone 50 mg at 20:00 Sunday, 02:00 and 08:00 Monday (mr-t0007), and diphenhydramine 50 mg at 08:00 (mr-t0008). He needs a driver. A corrected lab result arrived while I worked: his 10/14 creatinine is 2.8, not 0.98 (that was another patient's sample), so eGFR is about 24. I added 0.9% saline 500 mL IV at 08:00 (mr-t0019). He got a Spanish/English message (comm-t0012) and then a correction (comm-t0023), because the first one said his kidney test was normal. Urgent task for you about the newly found reduced kidney function (task-t0029).\n\n3. pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast. Ordered (sr-t0003). Her 10/04 ED visit documented acute kidney injury that hadn't returned to baseline. I ordered a creatinine before the scan (sr-t0006) and saline 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0009). I put metformin on hold (mr-00392) through the scan and at least 48 hours after; your task task-t0015 is to restart it only after a normal kidney recheck. An outside report arrived showing a moderate reaction to iopamidol in 2022, so I added premedication: prednisone at 00:00, 06:00 and 12:00 (mr-t0020), and diphenhydramine at 12:00 (mr-t0021). Messages comm-t0013, then a correction comm-t0024 saying she now needs a driver. Iopamidol is not on her allergy list yet; the catalog had no code for it, so it needs adding by hand.\n\n4. pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00, CT without contrast (stone protocol). Ordered as booked (sr-t0004); no prep needed. An outside report shows a mild iohexol reaction in 2024. I added it to her allergy list (alg-t0022); it doesn't affect a non-contrast scan. Message comm-t0014.\n\nNotes are signed for each patient, with addenda for the changes. The four new inbox items are closed. The older inbox items for other patients were not touched.",
